Every retained reaction is element-balanced. Retained NASA coefficients and transport parameters are identical to the parent; retained forward constants and net rates agree exactly at ten common test states (500–3500 K, 1/20 atm). Species cp is positive on a 101-temperature grid from 300 to 3500 K. No final candidate retains a >1%-scale NASA mid-temperature discontinuity under the audit's cp, h/RT and s/R criteria. Parent and several rejected larger candidates do have inherited jumps.

For the **408 final confirmation/external ignition integrations**, maximum relative internal-energy drift is 1.72e-8 and maximum elemental mass-fraction drift is 1.20e-12. Earlier development summaries did not all record these fields; they are not silently counted as passing this drift audit. Across 168 final confirmation/external flame profiles, relative mass-flux range is below 1.49e-8; endpoint enthalpy residual normalized by the audit's thermal scale is below 0.20%, and maximum endpoint elemental mass-fraction difference is below 2.93e-4. These residuals describe finite-grid/differential-diffusion solutions, separately from exact reaction stoichiometric balance.

Three parent synthetic post-ignition tails exceed some species' nominal 3500-K NASA range, reaching 3711 K. No development maximum-dT/dt ignition point exceeds 3500 K (largest 3125 K). This inherited thermodynamic extrapolation remains a limitation; it was not corrected by fitting.

## 6. Reproducibility, failures and stopping

See [REPRODUCE.md](REPRODUCE.md) for commands and an artifact map. Final model metadata lists every retained species and original zero-based reaction index. `results/candidate_freeze.json`, `results/rebuild_verification.json`, per-case inputs/outputs, raw traces/profiles, logs, downloaded papers/HTML and source URLs are retained. The custom scientific batch method is versioned as a trial skill with a pinned code hash and completed trusted execution receipts; registration and execution are distinct from proof of efficacy.

A final independent researcher source review checked the rich-acetylene composition, observed value, uncertainty, calculated deviations and primary/republished labels. It found no numerical correction in that scope and prompted clearer wording that multicomponent/Soret transport describes the simulations. The review is retained in `agents/01a0a625-c61e-7d91-97db-ca3f74e1a687/final_flame_interpretation_review.md`; it is a bounded review, not independent experimental or simulation replication.

Public access outcomes influenced coverage: SFCPD pages were usable; several hydrogen/CO ignition detail URLs returned 404. ReSpecTh's landing page was accessible but the attempted data route required registration; no account was requested. The public ChemKED repository was inspected but did not yield a focused C0–C3 shock dataset through that route. Original USC-II website/mirrors were unavailable. Primary paper retrieval therefore focused on Shao and Park, with older-method coverage explicitly incomplete.

Preserved unsuccessful work includes the carbon cutoff, overly aggressive graph thresholds, 48-species flame failure, incomplete pathway candidates, rejected v1 data parser, a remote submission rejected with ConnectionError (zero charged execution, then retried), and missing trace archives from two earlier large development jobs. Those jobs returned macroscopic per-case summaries; the reason some large trace archives were not returned is unknown. Final confirmation and external archives were all retrieved. A local audit aggregation initially assumed older summaries contained new conservation fields; that postprocessing error was corrected by explicitly reporting the 408 integrations that recorded them. No solver failure or missing field was converted into a scientific pass.

The search stops with three reproducible trade-offs, successful reserved synthetic tests, measured external limitations and numerical/physical checks. The 14 settled remote jobs plus one rejected submission charged 180,672 allocated core-seconds (50.2 core-hours), including allocated idle time; this is not an actual CPU-utilization measurement. The run did not exhaust its allowance. There is no evidence of global optimality, and further deletion would require new development evidence and a new reserved confirmation set. The recommended 58-species model is the most defensible broad tested choice; the 53- and 49-species mechanisms are provided as smaller, explicitly limited air-domain options. Experimental discrepancies and omitted domains remain unresolved.

